<title>UK: Rolls-Royce wins $450 mln Tupolev order.</title>
<headline>Rolls-Royce wins $450 mln Tupolev order.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rolls-Royce Plc said it had received an order worth up to $450 million to power a batch of Russian-built Tupolev airliners from the Kato Group of Egypt.  </p>
<p>The contract with Kato covers RB211-535 engines for 13 firm and 17 option aircraft ordered by the Cairo-based group.</p>
<p>Rolls-Royce said the deal represented the production launch of the Rolls-Royce-powered version of the Tupolev Tu-204.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
